  abstract={This article addresses the interval estimation problem for continuous systems with process disturbance and measurement noise under multirate discrete measurements. First, a dynamic observer is designed to provide state point estimation for the multirate measurement structure. Then, by merging the asynchronous measurement time sequences, interval estimation incorporating system state is achieved through point estimation error propagation analysis and peak-to-peak analysis. Further, an optimization problem is formulated to improve interval estimation accuracy. Compared with the existing interval estimation methods for continuous systems, the proposed method eliminates cooperative constraints and introduces a dynamic observer structure, which enhances the design freedom. Finally, the effectiveness of the proposed method is verified through simulation examples, with comparative experiments confirming its ability to generate tighter intervals.},
